Promote the first evidence-backed landing-to-checker conversion experiment after the clean post-integrity cohort reached 15 genuine landings with no new checker starts, uploads or analyses. The measured earliest funnel constraint is therefore landing/search-source to checker start.

This release adds a low-risk reversible decision-page entry treatment: static decision articles get a compact persistent call-to-action that explicitly moves readers from general guidance to checking their actual quote. The CTA routes to the existing homepage checker with a one-time hqc_start parameter that invokes the existing start control rather than introducing a new analysis path. QA traffic is excluded from auto-start behaviour. No evidence, certification, grant-eligibility, personal-data, payment, DNS or backend logic is changed.

Hypothesis: qualified search visitors landing on decision content are interested in evaluating a real quote but face unnecessary navigation friction before entering the checker. Reducing that handoff to one explicit action should produce the first clean checker starts without weakening product-independence guardrails.

